        "original_id": "88709982-5b76-55c9-aa1c-cc077a64ab96",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred von Tirpitz, Adolf Hitler, Karl Dönitz, Erich Raeder\n- Roles: naval leader, head of state of Germany, highest naval rank\n- Places: Germany\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred von Tirpitz was the earlier holder of Germany’s highest possible naval rank.\n- Before and during World War II, Erich Raeder was a naval leader in Germany and attained Germany’s highest possible naval rank.\n- Erich Raeder was later replaced by Karl Dönitz.\n- Karl Dönitz briefly succeeded Adolf Hitler as the head of state of Germany.",
